1
00:01:32,960 --> 00:01:35,060
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,280 --> 00:01:37,759
[Episode 5]

3
00:01:43,310 --> 00:01:44,200
Dad, go back.

4
00:01:45,950 --> 00:01:46,430
Son.

5
00:01:47,070 --> 00:01:48,120
I'm sorry.

6
00:01:49,150 --> 00:01:51,550
You were wronged at the village committee.

7
00:01:51,840 --> 00:01:53,170
I know it's hard for you.

8
00:01:55,350 --> 00:01:57,350
We have to submit to circumstances.

9
00:01:58,640 --> 00:02:00,300
I went to college for nothing.

10
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:01,950
Facing a village secretary...

11
00:02:01,950 --> 00:02:03,480
Don't sell yourself short.

12
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,230
You're destined for great things.

13
00:02:05,230 --> 00:02:06,810
Don't let a petty village official

14
00:02:06,810 --> 00:02:07,970
break your spirit.

15
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:10,710
Your name, Gaoyuan, means ''aiming high.''

16
00:02:10,710 --> 00:02:12,170
I named you with this hope.

17
00:02:12,910 --> 00:02:14,310
Don't let me down.

18
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:19,530
I'm leaving.

19
00:02:40,470 --> 00:02:42,520
How many people have you questioned?

20
00:02:42,520 --> 00:02:43,630
Over a hundred.

21
00:02:44,360 --> 00:02:46,360
But only two statements

22
00:02:46,360 --> 00:02:47,820
are relatively valuable.

23
00:02:47,870 --> 00:02:49,730
Mentor, do you think it's enough?

24
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:50,840
What do you think?

25
00:02:51,210 --> 00:02:52,360
I don't think it matters what I think.

26
00:02:52,360 --> 00:02:53,690
It's not up to me anyway.

27
00:02:53,750 --> 00:02:55,520
Just pretend you are the judge.

28
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:01,430
Then I don't think Liu Erlin

29
00:03:01,430 --> 00:03:02,560
committed robbery.

30
00:03:04,710 --> 00:03:05,520
But...

31
00:03:08,710 --> 00:03:09,470
His...

32
00:03:11,950 --> 00:03:12,820
What I want to hear

33
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:14,480
is what comes after the "but."

34
00:03:14,590 --> 00:03:15,850
What do you want to say?

35
00:03:19,560 --> 00:03:22,120
But there's one thing
that hasn't been verified.

36
00:03:22,120 --> 00:03:23,250
I never met Laishun.

37
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:24,680
So as for Liu Erlin's claim

38
00:03:24,680 --> 00:03:26,210
that he mistook the person,

39
00:03:26,710 --> 00:03:27,370
I have no way

40
00:03:27,370 --> 00:03:29,370
to prove whether it's true or false.

41
00:03:30,800 --> 00:03:32,000
Didn't you say

42
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:34,310
we should presume all defendants

43
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:35,520
are innocent?

44
00:03:37,120 --> 00:03:37,470
What?

45
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:39,810
You're feeling uneasy now?

46
00:03:40,630 --> 00:03:42,960
You don't even believe yourself anymore?

47
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:44,000
Not really.

48
00:03:50,520 --> 00:03:50,980
Mentor,

49
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:53,010
when is the next court session?

50
00:03:53,240 --> 00:03:54,170
What's the rush?

51
00:03:55,590 --> 00:03:57,790
Cases like this don't need to be rushed.

52
00:03:57,800 --> 00:03:59,260
A little delay won't hurt.

53
00:04:08,190 --> 00:04:08,720
Yizhong.

54
00:04:10,430 --> 00:04:11,360
I think you're

55
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,710
getting a bit obsessed.

56
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:21,680
Mentor.

57
00:04:23,270 --> 00:04:25,120
I want to see Liu Erlin.

58
00:04:25,830 --> 00:04:27,230
Can you arrange it for me?

59
00:04:28,390 --> 00:04:29,120
Mr. Zhang.

60
00:04:29,600 --> 00:04:30,480
What's going on?

61
00:04:30,480 --> 00:04:31,270
Why's it taking so long?

62
00:04:31,270 --> 00:04:32,260
When am I getting released?

63
00:04:32,260 --> 00:04:34,070
The government hasn't forgotten me, right?

64
00:04:34,070 --> 00:04:35,670
Look, you've gained weight.

65
00:04:36,800 --> 00:04:37,830
Staying a few more days

66
00:04:37,830 --> 00:04:38,760
will do you good.

67
00:04:39,510 --> 00:04:40,630
What are you talking about?

68
00:04:40,630 --> 00:04:41,450
If everything were fine, who'd want...

69
00:04:41,450 --> 00:04:43,450
Keep your voice down. Sit properly.

70
00:04:46,120 --> 00:04:46,720
If everything were fine,

71
00:04:46,720 --> 00:04:47,920
who'd want to be here?

72
00:04:49,920 --> 00:04:50,480
Go ahead.

73
00:04:51,560 --> 00:04:52,159
Liu Erlin,

74
00:04:52,990 --> 00:04:53,870
we are here

75
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:56,180
to gather some additional information.

76
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:57,950
Just answer whatever we ask.

77
00:04:57,950 --> 00:04:59,800
If you remember, say you remember.

78
00:04:59,800 --> 00:05:01,240
If you don't, say you don't.

79
00:05:01,240 --> 00:05:02,770
But you must tell the truth.

80
00:05:02,800 --> 00:05:03,600
Don't lie.

81
00:05:04,090 --> 00:05:05,740
I have never lied.

82
00:05:05,770 --> 00:05:07,310
It was those officers who framed me.

83
00:05:07,310 --> 00:05:08,430
Alright.

84
00:05:08,630 --> 00:05:09,960
Just answer what we ask.

85
00:05:11,680 --> 00:05:12,280
Liu Erlin,

86
00:05:12,750 --> 00:05:14,360
how many people have you actually poked

87
00:05:14,360 --> 00:05:15,820
with that toy gun of yours?

88
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:16,560
Two.

89
00:05:17,390 --> 00:05:18,120
Who are they?

90
00:05:20,120 --> 00:05:21,800
I've said this several times.

91
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:22,600
Why are you...

92
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,390
Then say it again.

93
00:05:24,750 --> 00:05:26,210
Tired of using your mouth?

94
00:05:29,390 --> 00:05:30,160
One is

95
00:05:30,160 --> 00:05:32,150
Fang who sells lumber at the market.

96
00:05:32,150 --> 00:05:33,610
The other one I don't know.

97
00:05:34,290 --> 00:05:36,240
I thought I knew him.

98
00:05:36,270 --> 00:05:37,040
I mistook him for someone else.

99
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:37,830
Otherwise I wouldn't have

100
00:05:37,830 --> 00:05:39,159
played that joke on him.

101
00:05:39,430 --> 00:05:40,950
Who did you take him for?

102
00:05:41,630 --> 00:05:42,390
Laishun.

103
00:05:43,430 --> 00:05:43,960
Laishun?

104
00:05:48,600 --> 00:05:49,830
Are you close

105
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:51,040
with Laishun?

106
00:05:51,270 --> 00:05:51,830
Yeah.

107
00:05:52,240 --> 00:05:53,360
We are from the same village.

108
00:05:53,360 --> 00:05:55,290
He helps load lumber at the market.

109
00:05:57,120 --> 00:05:58,310
Then why weren't any of these details

110
00:05:58,310 --> 00:06:00,000
you mentioned

111
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:01,660
in your previous statements?

112
00:06:02,630 --> 00:06:06,120
Well... nobody asked me about it.

113
00:06:06,560 --> 00:06:07,830
How would I know what to say

114
00:06:07,830 --> 00:06:08,890
and what not to say?

115
00:06:09,750 --> 00:06:11,840
The police and the procuratorate
didn't ask?

116
00:06:11,840 --> 00:06:12,350
No.

117
00:06:12,380 --> 00:06:13,520
I said I mistook him for someone else,

118
00:06:13,520 --> 00:06:15,450
but they just wouldn't believe me.

119
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:17,130
Alright.

120
00:06:18,950 --> 00:06:19,480
Yizhong,

121
00:06:20,260 --> 00:06:21,520
ask the key questions.

122
00:06:24,240 --> 00:06:25,210
This victim,

123
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:25,920
the one

124
00:06:25,950 --> 00:06:27,810
you mistook for Laishun that day,

125
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:28,950
what was he wearing?

126
00:06:28,950 --> 00:06:30,210
Do you still remember?

127
00:06:31,270 --> 00:06:31,830
On top,

128
00:06:32,300 --> 00:06:33,909
he was wearing a kinda worn-out

129
00:06:33,909 --> 00:06:35,040
army-green jacket.

130
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:36,920
Blue pants, and Liberation shoes.

131
00:06:36,920 --> 00:06:37,870
He was also wearing a peaked cap.

132
00:06:37,870 --> 00:06:39,070
Laishun loves wearing peaked caps.

133
00:06:39,070 --> 00:06:41,400
Otherwise, I wouldn't have mistaken him.

134
00:06:42,750 --> 00:06:44,810
That guy also had sloping shoulders.

135
00:06:45,310 --> 00:06:46,440
Sloping shoulders?

136
00:06:51,720 --> 00:06:52,980
Who's joking with you?

137
00:06:53,390 --> 00:06:55,010
What do you mean, mistook the person?

138
00:06:55,010 --> 00:06:56,050
He held a gun

139
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:56,810
against my waist.

140
00:06:56,810 --> 00:06:58,240
That was the bag I had the money in.

141
00:06:58,240 --> 00:06:59,970
If that's not robbery, what is?

142
00:07:00,040 --> 00:07:01,270
Your court better not take bribes
or pervert justice.

143
00:07:01,270 --> 00:07:02,200
I'm telling you.

144
00:07:04,720 --> 00:07:06,320
His heart's never been good.

145
00:07:06,720 --> 00:07:08,850
This whole thing made him really sick.

146
00:07:09,880 --> 00:07:10,480
Comrade.

147
00:07:10,500 --> 00:07:11,760
Please don't mind him.

148
00:07:14,630 --> 00:07:15,160
Sir.

149
00:07:15,430 --> 00:07:16,890
Can I take a picture of you?

150
00:07:17,390 --> 00:07:18,190
What picture?

151
00:07:18,390 --> 00:07:19,800
Our leader ordered it.

152
00:07:20,120 --> 00:07:21,450
I need it to report back.

153
00:07:21,510 --> 00:07:22,570
Please cooperate.

154
00:07:22,870 --> 00:07:23,360
I won't.

155
00:07:26,190 --> 00:07:27,120
Why so stubborn?

156
00:07:28,830 --> 00:07:29,950
Look, I even brought

157
00:07:29,950 --> 00:07:31,130
the camera.

158
00:07:32,630 --> 00:07:33,490
How about this?

159
00:07:33,720 --> 00:07:34,240
I'll take a picture

160
00:07:34,240 --> 00:07:35,270
of both of you here.

161
00:07:35,270 --> 00:07:37,390
I'll have it developed
and bring it over to you.

162
00:07:37,390 --> 00:07:38,630
Then let me take a single picture of you,

163
00:07:38,630 --> 00:07:39,510
so I can report back.

164
00:07:39,510 --> 00:07:39,920
Okay?

165
00:07:40,390 --> 00:07:41,360
Ma'am, okay?

166
00:07:42,950 --> 00:07:43,409
Come on.

167
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:44,630
Ma'am, lean over here a bit.

168
00:07:44,630 --> 00:07:45,090
Come on.

169
00:07:50,870 --> 00:07:52,430
A little more.

170
00:07:52,450 --> 00:07:53,250
Just a little.

171
00:07:53,360 --> 00:07:55,920
Ready. One, two, three.

172
00:08:05,680 --> 00:08:06,280
All right.

173
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:08,240
Everyone is here,

174
00:08:08,680 --> 00:08:10,080
let's start the meeting.

175
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:11,800
Today,

176
00:08:12,310 --> 00:08:13,770
we will discuss two cases.

177
00:08:13,800 --> 00:08:14,510
One is

178
00:08:15,270 --> 00:08:17,310
the murder case handled by Fang.

179
00:08:18,190 --> 00:08:18,920
The other is

180
00:08:19,750 --> 00:08:21,560
the theft case handled by Xu.

181
00:08:22,240 --> 00:08:22,680
Fang,

182
00:08:23,270 --> 00:08:24,720
let's start with your case.

183
00:08:24,720 --> 00:08:25,190
Tell us—

184
00:08:25,440 --> 00:08:27,400
what is the opinion

185
00:08:27,430 --> 00:08:28,010
of your collegial panel?

186
00:08:28,010 --> 00:08:29,840
After careful deliberation

187
00:08:29,870 --> 00:08:31,060
by the collegial panel

188
00:08:31,060 --> 00:08:32,049
and a vote

189
00:08:32,080 --> 00:08:33,010
by show of hands,

190
00:08:33,480 --> 00:08:34,679
the decision was 2-1:

191
00:08:35,480 --> 00:08:37,280
death sentence with a reprieve.

192
00:08:42,030 --> 00:08:42,549
Fang,

193
00:08:43,320 --> 00:08:44,000
I know

194
00:08:45,270 --> 00:08:47,530
you've had a lot of family issues lately.

195
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:48,840
You're very busy,

196
00:08:49,240 --> 00:08:50,550
feeling a bit tired and stressed.

197
00:08:50,550 --> 00:08:51,550
Court Pres. Ding,

198
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:53,960
our decision

199
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:55,360
is actually based

200
00:08:55,360 --> 00:08:56,620
on very solid grounds.

201
00:09:01,120 --> 00:09:01,720
All right.

202
00:09:03,720 --> 00:09:04,920
Tell us your reasons.

203
00:09:05,180 --> 00:09:06,930
The defendant, Qiu Agui,

204
00:09:06,960 --> 00:09:08,630
faced increasingly severe abuse every day—

205
00:09:08,630 --> 00:09:10,630
that's a well‑known fact.

206
00:09:11,150 --> 00:09:12,270
And her three children

207
00:09:12,270 --> 00:09:14,270
were obviously threatened as well.

208
00:09:14,840 --> 00:09:16,100
There's another fact:

209
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:17,440
even though Qiu Agui

210
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:18,600
doesn't admit it

211
00:09:18,600 --> 00:09:19,960
to protect her daughter,

212
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:21,320
I believe it's true.

213
00:09:22,150 --> 00:09:23,010
Huang Liancang

214
00:09:23,440 --> 00:09:25,440
deliberately harmed his daughter.

215
00:09:25,590 --> 00:09:26,920
From this perspective,

216
00:09:27,080 --> 00:09:27,750
Qiu Agui

217
00:09:27,960 --> 00:09:29,270
was protecting her daughter

218
00:09:29,270 --> 00:09:30,270
from being raped.

219
00:09:30,870 --> 00:09:32,200
So here's our thinking:

220
00:09:32,790 --> 00:09:33,840
if we can persuade

221
00:09:34,030 --> 00:09:35,120
Qiu Agui's family

222
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:37,200
to offer more compensation,

223
00:09:37,670 --> 00:09:39,150
and the victim's family

224
00:09:39,630 --> 00:09:40,890
is willing to forgive,

225
00:09:41,360 --> 00:09:42,320
then for this case,

226
00:09:42,320 --> 00:09:43,840
death sentence with a reprieve

227
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:46,640
would be entirely appropriate.
Court Pres. Ding.

228
00:09:51,600 --> 00:09:52,240
Fang.

229
00:09:54,150 --> 00:09:55,030
Do you know that

230
00:09:55,670 --> 00:09:57,030
our county court

231
00:09:57,790 --> 00:09:59,910
has absolutely no jurisdiction

232
00:10:01,790 --> 00:10:02,790
over this case?

233
00:10:04,910 --> 00:10:05,440
I know.

234
00:10:05,790 --> 00:10:06,550
You know?

235
00:10:07,910 --> 00:10:08,640
Fang Shumei,

236
00:10:09,670 --> 00:10:10,270
you know

237
00:10:10,980 --> 00:10:12,150
everything.

238
00:10:12,510 --> 00:10:13,170
But you also

239
00:10:13,790 --> 00:10:15,510
know nothing.

240
00:10:16,230 --> 00:10:16,960
Understand?

241
00:10:17,320 --> 00:10:18,320
Court Pres. Ding,

242
00:10:19,320 --> 00:10:21,580
I understand the court's difficulties.

243
00:10:21,750 --> 00:10:24,200
I also understand the pressure
from the county government.

244
00:10:24,200 --> 00:10:25,630
But I understand better

245
00:10:26,270 --> 00:10:27,270
the despair

246
00:10:27,270 --> 00:10:28,270
of a cornered woman

247
00:10:28,270 --> 00:10:29,470
beaten day after day.

248
00:10:30,870 --> 00:10:32,470
And who wouldn't understand

249
00:10:33,160 --> 00:10:34,000
a mother's heart—

250
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:35,510
willing to die

251
00:10:35,510 --> 00:10:36,370
rather than let

252
00:10:37,390 --> 00:10:39,520
her daughter's reputation be ruined?

253
00:10:43,120 --> 00:10:44,120
Court Pres. Ding,

254
00:10:44,790 --> 00:10:45,590
I implore you.

255
00:10:46,960 --> 00:10:48,090
I implore everyone.

256
00:10:52,240 --> 00:10:54,240
Please put yourselves in her shoes.

257
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:01,890
Alright.

258
00:11:03,080 --> 00:11:03,840
We all know the opinion

259
00:11:03,840 --> 00:11:05,170
of the collegial panel.

260
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:06,240
You may leave.

261
00:11:07,550 --> 00:11:09,030
Let Adjudication Committee discuss it.

262
00:11:09,030 --> 00:11:10,030
Court Pres. Ding,

263
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:12,200
may I attend the entire discussion?

264
00:11:38,480 --> 00:11:39,480
Court Pres. Ding.

265
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:40,600
Court Pres. Ding.

266
00:11:41,510 --> 00:11:42,790
Shall we discuss

267
00:11:42,790 --> 00:11:43,670
our case first?

268
00:11:45,320 --> 00:11:45,850
Go ahead.

269
00:11:46,150 --> 00:11:48,120
The defendant, a cashier at her workplace,

270
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:49,240
embezzled funds under her custody,

271
00:11:49,240 --> 00:11:51,030
and the amount involved
is especially huge.

272
00:11:51,030 --> 00:11:51,910
The procuratorate

273
00:11:51,910 --> 00:11:53,910
has recommended the death penalty.

274
00:11:53,910 --> 00:11:55,640
Our collegial panel's opinion

275
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:57,280
is consistent with theirs—

276
00:11:57,600 --> 00:11:58,460
death penalty.

277
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:07,390
Have some water.

278
00:12:07,390 --> 00:12:07,960
That's so kind of you.

279
00:12:07,960 --> 00:12:08,560
Thank you.

280
00:12:09,240 --> 00:12:10,170
Secretary Zhao.

281
00:12:10,410 --> 00:12:11,930
I just wanted to ask—

282
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:13,890
does Laishun have no other family?

283
00:12:14,150 --> 00:12:15,030
No.

284
00:12:15,840 --> 00:12:16,440
Besides,

285
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:18,560
what could his family prove?

286
00:12:20,200 --> 00:12:21,030
Then,

287
00:12:21,240 --> 00:12:22,510
what does Laishun look like?

288
00:12:22,510 --> 00:12:23,310
How tall is he?

289
00:12:25,670 --> 00:12:26,200
Not tall.

290
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,270
A bit skinny.

291
00:12:28,910 --> 00:12:29,640
Small eyes.

292
00:12:30,750 --> 00:12:32,000
Other than that,

293
00:12:33,120 --> 00:12:34,850
there's really nothing to say.

294
00:12:35,670 --> 00:12:36,670
Laishun

295
00:12:37,320 --> 00:12:38,600
is a bit cowardly.

296
00:12:39,150 --> 00:12:41,040
He doesn't stand out wherever he is.

297
00:12:41,040 --> 00:12:42,170
If he doesn't speak,

298
00:12:42,360 --> 00:12:44,160
it's like he doesn't even exist.

299
00:12:45,510 --> 00:12:47,910
Does he have sloped shoulders from behind?

300
00:12:49,360 --> 00:12:50,390
It's possible.

301
00:12:52,120 --> 00:12:53,450
I never really noticed.

302
00:12:57,030 --> 00:12:58,490
Does he usually wear a hat?

303
00:13:01,360 --> 00:13:02,150
No,

304
00:13:03,150 --> 00:13:04,150
not that I recall.

305
00:13:08,630 --> 00:13:09,560
Secretary Zhao,

306
00:13:09,840 --> 00:13:10,640
is it possible

307
00:13:11,320 --> 00:13:12,990
that you have a photo of Laishun here?

308
00:13:12,990 --> 00:13:13,990
Let me take a look.

309
00:13:14,330 --> 00:13:15,590
Country folks like us,

310
00:13:15,720 --> 00:13:18,180
who could afford
to get their picture taken?

311
00:13:18,510 --> 00:13:20,840
This is the only photo
I've ever had taken—

312
00:13:21,440 --> 00:13:24,120
snapped just last month
when we were repairing the dam,

313
00:13:24,120 --> 00:13:26,230
all thanks to the local officials.

314
00:13:27,490 --> 00:13:28,410
Here.

315
00:13:28,630 --> 00:13:29,690
Have some water.

316
00:13:30,240 --> 00:13:31,170
You're too kind.

317
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:34,080
Eat some peanuts.

318
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:34,910
Alright, alright. I've got plenty here.

319
00:13:34,910 --> 00:13:35,480
We don't have anything special.

320
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:36,030
That's plenty.

321
00:13:36,030 --> 00:13:37,480
That's plenty, Secretary Zhao.

322
00:13:37,480 --> 00:13:38,030
Okay.

323
00:13:41,080 --> 00:13:43,010
Secretary Zhao, no need to see me out.

324
00:13:43,010 --> 00:13:44,920
For Liu Erlin's case,

325
00:13:45,030 --> 00:13:46,560
you've worked really hard,

326
00:13:46,680 --> 00:13:47,650
You travelled

327
00:13:47,790 --> 00:13:48,720
so many times.

328
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:51,400
If you need any help in the future,

329
00:13:51,670 --> 00:13:52,730
just give me a call.

330
00:13:53,200 --> 00:13:53,550
Okay.

331
00:13:54,910 --> 00:13:56,080
You still have to take the mountain road.

332
00:13:56,080 --> 00:13:57,120
If it gets completely dark,

333
00:13:57,120 --> 00:13:58,150
it will be very dangerous.

334
00:13:58,150 --> 00:13:58,680
So I won't

335
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:00,370
keep you for dinner.

336
00:14:00,670 --> 00:14:01,800
I'll be leaving now.

337
00:14:07,940 --> 00:14:09,270
Secretary, how are you?

338
00:14:51,600 --> 00:14:52,530
Secretary Zhao.

339
00:14:53,870 --> 00:14:55,130
Why are you back again?

340
00:14:55,200 --> 00:14:56,260
Look at this photo.

341
00:14:56,320 --> 00:14:56,980
Take a look.

342
00:14:57,200 --> 00:14:57,550
Look.

343
00:14:57,790 --> 00:14:58,390
Which one?

344
00:15:01,200 --> 00:15:02,080
Laishun.

345
00:15:05,390 --> 00:15:06,320
Is this Laishun?

346
00:15:12,120 --> 00:15:12,650
It's him.

347
00:15:12,960 --> 00:15:13,360
Right?

348
00:15:13,480 --> 00:15:14,280
It's Laishun.

349
00:15:15,120 --> 00:15:16,550
He really is wearing a hat.

350
00:15:16,550 --> 00:15:17,750
I completely forgot.

351
00:15:18,270 --> 00:15:19,070
Comrade Chen,

352
00:15:19,150 --> 00:15:20,510
this photo has been hanging here
for almost two months.

353
00:15:20,510 --> 00:15:21,360
I never even noticed.

354
00:15:21,360 --> 00:15:23,020
How did you spot it at a glance?

355
00:15:23,200 --> 00:15:24,750
Does he always wear this outfit?

356
00:15:24,750 --> 00:15:25,600
Yes, he does.

357
00:15:25,960 --> 00:15:26,750
A country man

358
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:29,010
only has one outfit all year round.

359
00:15:29,670 --> 00:15:30,600
Secretary Zhao,

360
00:15:30,720 --> 00:15:32,250
can I take a picture of this?

361
00:15:32,840 --> 00:15:34,020
Yeah. Go ahead.

362
00:15:38,150 --> 00:15:38,950
Comrade Chen.

363
00:15:40,080 --> 00:15:42,880
You went through all that trouble
to find Laishun.

364
00:15:43,390 --> 00:15:44,270
What's the use?

365
00:16:01,390 --> 00:16:02,080
Mentor.

366
00:16:02,360 --> 00:16:02,960
Mentor.

367
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:06,360
Why are you here?

368
00:16:13,030 --> 00:16:13,560
Let's go.

369
00:16:15,320 --> 00:16:16,720
I'll treat you to drinks.

370
00:16:17,200 --> 00:16:18,750
Mentor, aren't you going home?

371
00:16:18,750 --> 00:16:20,210
I'll go home late tonight.

372
00:16:20,720 --> 00:16:21,360
Right.

373
00:16:27,440 --> 00:16:28,790
The Adjudication Committee's ruling
on Qiu Agui

374
00:16:28,790 --> 00:16:29,340
is out.

375
00:16:34,670 --> 00:16:35,530
Death penalty.

376
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:51,770
That day I went to Qiu Agui's house.

377
00:16:54,840 --> 00:16:56,370
I almost asked her daughter

378
00:16:58,550 --> 00:16:59,360
if she'd be willing

379
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:00,820
to testify for her mother.

380
00:17:04,920 --> 00:17:05,849
I was that close.

381
00:17:09,640 --> 00:17:11,310
I pinched my thigh until it turned red

382
00:17:11,310 --> 00:17:12,440
to hold myself back.

383
00:17:24,589 --> 00:17:26,109
I hate myself.

384
00:17:27,450 --> 00:17:28,319
I feel that I am

385
00:17:28,349 --> 00:17:29,590
extremely cowardly,

386
00:17:30,440 --> 00:17:31,110
spineless,

387
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:32,930
and disgusting.

388
00:17:34,550 --> 00:17:35,590
Count me in too.

389
00:17:36,730 --> 00:17:38,440
Fang Shumei, the person
you once called Mentor,

390
00:17:38,440 --> 00:17:39,550
isn't that right?

391
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:44,240
No, Mentor.

392
00:17:45,360 --> 00:17:46,790
Yingjie is just too upset.

393
00:17:46,790 --> 00:17:47,480
She drank too much.

394
00:17:47,480 --> 00:17:48,740
Don't take it to heart.

395
00:17:51,720 --> 00:17:52,310
Yingjie,

396
00:17:52,780 --> 00:17:53,710
we're all upset.

397
00:17:54,480 --> 00:17:55,510
But have you ever thought,

398
00:17:55,510 --> 00:17:56,720
what if her daughter's testimony

399
00:17:56,720 --> 00:17:57,850
doesn't help at all?

400
00:17:58,080 --> 00:17:58,960
Then Qiu Agui...

401
00:17:58,960 --> 00:18:00,680
Stop smoothing things over.

402
00:18:00,920 --> 00:18:01,510
I'm not.

403
00:18:02,110 --> 00:18:04,160
How can you calculate things that way?

404
00:18:04,160 --> 00:18:05,790
That's a human life, Lihui.

405
00:18:05,790 --> 00:18:06,640
A human life.

406
00:18:06,660 --> 00:18:07,990
I just feel that anyone,

407
00:18:08,240 --> 00:18:09,500
no matter who they are,

408
00:18:09,580 --> 00:18:10,630
would find it hard

409
00:18:10,650 --> 00:18:11,830
to deal with so many problems.

410
00:18:11,830 --> 00:18:12,890
It's not like that.

411
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:14,350
This is not the problem

412
00:18:14,350 --> 00:18:16,030
we should be facing at all.

413
00:18:18,400 --> 00:18:19,350
Many problems

414
00:18:20,310 --> 00:18:21,750
cannot be solved by law.

415
00:18:22,310 --> 00:18:23,000
In this world,

416
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,600
there really are many things

417
00:18:25,510 --> 00:18:26,680
where the law is the last resort.

418
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:28,810
You're trying to convince me, aren't you?

419
00:18:28,810 --> 00:18:29,510
So that you yourself

420
00:18:29,510 --> 00:18:31,110
can feel less guilty, right?

421
00:18:34,750 --> 00:18:35,110
Okay.

422
00:18:36,110 --> 00:18:37,000
Then let's talk

423
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:37,830
about the law.

424
00:18:40,160 --> 00:18:42,090
Is that little girl a victim or not?

425
00:18:42,720 --> 00:18:44,650
Should she be protected by the law?

426
00:18:45,240 --> 00:18:46,700
Does Qiu Agui's situation

427
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,600
warrant a lighter sentence?

428
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:49,840
Can we spare her life?

429
00:18:51,030 --> 00:18:52,070
To protect the little girl,

430
00:18:52,070 --> 00:18:54,000
do we have to sacrifice the mother?

431
00:18:54,240 --> 00:18:54,790
What if

432
00:18:55,270 --> 00:18:56,480
those two bastards were still alive,

433
00:18:56,480 --> 00:18:57,000
would we still have to

434
00:18:57,000 --> 00:18:57,720
compromise

435
00:18:57,720 --> 00:18:58,720
and protect them?

436
00:19:02,830 --> 00:19:05,750
Qiu Agui could have lived,

437
00:19:07,110 --> 00:19:08,550
but we didn't even grant her

438
00:19:08,550 --> 00:19:10,410
a death sentence with a reprieve.

439
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:14,000
No.

440
00:19:14,630 --> 00:19:15,240
Not us.

441
00:19:16,030 --> 00:19:16,680
It's them.

442
00:19:17,270 --> 00:19:18,930
The Adjudication Committee.

443
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:20,480
Court Pres. Ding.

444
00:19:27,830 --> 00:19:29,760
Mentor, you're actually useless.

445
00:19:29,960 --> 00:19:30,790
We're all useless.

446
00:19:30,790 --> 00:19:32,070
We're all good-for-nothings.

447
00:19:32,070 --> 00:19:32,650
Yingjie.

448
00:19:32,910 --> 00:19:35,440
You have no right
to speak to Mentor like that.

449
00:19:40,030 --> 00:19:40,490
Mentor.

450
00:19:42,870 --> 00:19:44,160
Did I say something wrong?

451
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:45,360
You said it very well.

452
00:19:50,270 --> 00:19:51,720
Did I do something wrong?

453
00:19:56,510 --> 00:19:57,570
You did perfectly.

454
00:20:01,070 --> 00:20:02,400
Absolutely perfectly.

455
00:20:10,160 --> 00:20:10,640
Mentor.

456
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:12,000
Going back this late,

457
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:13,000
won't that guy

458
00:20:13,000 --> 00:20:14,200
give you any trouble?

459
00:20:18,880 --> 00:20:21,010
Have you never thought about leaving?

460
00:20:23,160 --> 00:20:24,560
Since the day I came back,

461
00:20:25,720 --> 00:20:27,450
I never thought about leaving.

462
00:20:35,200 --> 00:20:35,590
Alright.

463
00:20:35,590 --> 00:20:37,120
I'll see you off here today.

464
00:20:37,550 --> 00:20:37,880
Okay.

465
00:20:38,350 --> 00:20:38,720
Okay.

466
00:20:38,920 --> 00:20:39,550
Xia,

467
00:20:40,340 --> 00:20:41,790
you drank too much today.

468
00:20:41,830 --> 00:20:43,490
Go back and get some good rest.

469
00:20:43,880 --> 00:20:45,070
Go easy on the drinks from now on.

470
00:20:45,070 --> 00:20:45,790
I'm leaving.

471
00:20:45,790 --> 00:20:46,750
Take care, Ms. Fang.

472
00:20:46,750 --> 00:20:47,550
Goodbye, Mei.

473
00:20:47,750 --> 00:20:48,590
Mentor,

474
00:20:49,000 --> 00:20:50,110
don't worry.

475
00:21:01,030 --> 00:21:02,200
Smells so good.

476
00:21:03,830 --> 00:21:05,070
Who put it on me?

477
00:21:27,790 --> 00:21:28,320
Let's go.

478
00:21:28,400 --> 00:21:29,460
Let's go, Yizhong.

479
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:30,930
Yizhong.

480
00:21:31,720 --> 00:21:32,720
I didn't expect you city folks

481
00:21:32,720 --> 00:21:33,980
could ride a tricycle.

482
00:21:34,240 --> 00:21:35,240
It's hard to ride.

483
00:21:35,720 --> 00:21:37,120
I learned when I was a kid.

484
00:21:39,400 --> 00:21:41,460
I heard your dad is a presiding judge.

485
00:21:42,200 --> 00:21:43,200
Who told you that?

486
00:21:43,200 --> 00:21:44,200
My dad is a barber.

487
00:21:54,270 --> 00:21:55,270
Court Pres. Ding.

488
00:21:55,650 --> 00:21:56,550
The gatekeeper asked me to let you know

489
00:21:56,550 --> 00:21:58,030
that there are too many observers today.

490
00:21:58,030 --> 00:21:59,490
Something might go wrong.

491
00:22:00,070 --> 00:22:01,730
Then don't let anyone else in.

492
00:22:02,200 --> 00:22:02,530
Okay.

493
00:22:03,270 --> 00:22:04,270
Send two bailiffs

494
00:22:04,960 --> 00:22:06,750
to protect those two lawyers.

495
00:22:07,310 --> 00:22:07,680
Okay.

496
00:22:08,240 --> 00:22:09,170
Spread the word—

497
00:22:10,270 --> 00:22:12,400
anyone who disrupts court order today

498
00:22:13,310 --> 00:22:14,310
will be arrested.

499
00:22:14,690 --> 00:22:17,020
Why is the rape case being tried
in public?

500
00:22:17,270 --> 00:22:18,440
It's the Strike-Hard Campaign period.

501
00:22:18,440 --> 00:22:19,200
Special cases get special treatment.

502
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:19,550
Yes.

503
00:22:28,550 --> 00:22:30,000
Oh, Ding.

504
00:22:31,640 --> 00:22:33,000
You still have to

505
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:36,180
take the fall for this.

506
00:22:51,400 --> 00:22:52,440
What are you doing?

507
00:22:52,440 --> 00:22:53,480
I brought this on purpose.

508
00:22:53,480 --> 00:22:54,270
If anyone throws things at Li Xiang later,

509
00:22:54,270 --> 00:22:55,270
I'll throw it at them.

510
00:22:55,270 --> 00:22:56,590
Tit for tat, right?

511
00:22:57,070 --> 00:22:58,000
Really?

512
00:22:58,160 --> 00:22:58,680
Yeah.

513
00:22:59,160 --> 00:22:59,690
I just...

514
00:23:00,310 --> 00:23:00,970
Give me one.

515
00:23:01,350 --> 00:23:02,110
You're gonna throw too?

516
00:23:02,110 --> 00:23:03,000
Throw it hard.

517
00:23:04,030 --> 00:23:04,830
Confiscated.

518
00:23:04,830 --> 00:23:05,590
What?

519
00:23:05,930 --> 00:23:07,200
What do you mean confiscated?

520
00:23:07,200 --> 00:23:08,070
Why did you confiscate my ammo?

521
00:23:08,070 --> 00:23:08,720
Alright, stop arguing.

522
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:09,240
Don't make trouble

523
00:23:09,240 --> 00:23:10,240
in court, okay?

524
00:23:10,310 --> 00:23:10,750
You...

525
00:23:15,200 --> 00:23:15,960
What are you doing?

526
00:23:15,960 --> 00:23:17,290
Mind your own business.

527
00:23:17,720 --> 00:23:18,350
Where are you going?

528
00:23:18,350 --> 00:23:18,960
What are you doing?

529
00:23:18,960 --> 00:23:19,880
I've got one more.

530
00:23:19,880 --> 00:23:20,790
I've got one more.

531
00:23:20,790 --> 00:23:21,240
Don't.

532
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:34,200
For good luck.

533
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:36,440
Loyal at heart, prepared for all outcomes.

534
00:23:36,440 --> 00:23:36,900
Take it.

535
00:23:42,070 --> 00:23:42,960
Look at them.

536
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:45,210
If you plead not guilty,

537
00:23:45,350 --> 00:23:46,750
they'll never let us off.

538
00:23:48,310 --> 00:23:49,310
Plead not guilty?

539
00:23:50,870 --> 00:23:51,830
You've got guts.

540
00:23:52,480 --> 00:23:54,030
Hey, uh... Comrade.

541
00:23:54,590 --> 00:23:55,440
Take him out.

542
00:23:56,160 --> 00:23:56,350
Okay.

543
00:23:56,350 --> 00:23:56,790
Get out.

544
00:23:56,790 --> 00:23:57,310
Take me out?

545
00:23:57,310 --> 00:23:57,790
Out.

546
00:23:57,880 --> 00:23:58,210
Move.

547
00:23:58,550 --> 00:23:58,960
Lu,

548
00:23:59,200 --> 00:24:00,160
don't let Court Pres. Ding punish me.

549
00:24:00,160 --> 00:24:00,830
I know.

550
00:24:01,680 --> 00:24:02,210
Let's go.

551
00:24:02,920 --> 00:24:04,790
I guess it's fine for me to be here,
right?

552
00:24:04,790 --> 00:24:05,920
Lawyer Wang.

553
00:24:06,070 --> 00:24:07,110
What are you doing?

554
00:24:07,110 --> 00:24:08,190
Who are you talking to?

555
00:24:08,190 --> 00:24:09,070
I'm talking to you.

556
00:24:09,070 --> 00:24:09,610
I'm talking to you.

557
00:24:09,610 --> 00:24:10,870
Get down here. Come on.

558
00:24:15,060 --> 00:24:15,710
Order!

559
00:24:16,200 --> 00:24:17,000
All rise!

560
00:24:21,830 --> 00:24:22,430
Be seated.

561
00:24:34,070 --> 00:24:36,400
The Nanyu County People's Court

562
00:24:37,240 --> 00:24:38,700
now holds a public hearing

563
00:24:39,400 --> 00:24:41,400
for the case prosecuted

564
00:24:41,590 --> 00:24:43,350
by the Nanyu County People's Procuratorate

565
00:24:43,350 --> 00:24:45,080
against Qiao Zhiliang for rape

566
00:24:45,200 --> 00:24:46,480
resulting in death.

567
00:24:47,000 --> 00:24:48,330
Court is now in session.

568
00:24:49,030 --> 00:24:51,230
Bring in the defendant, Qiao Zhiliang.

569
00:24:59,160 --> 00:24:59,860
Step back!

570
00:25:00,160 --> 00:25:00,760
Step back!

571
00:25:01,030 --> 00:25:02,290
Maintain court order!

572
00:25:02,550 --> 00:25:03,080
Sit down!

573
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:12,240
Order!

574
00:25:12,400 --> 00:25:13,200
Order! Order!

575
00:25:13,440 --> 00:25:14,160
Maintain court order!

576
00:25:14,160 --> 00:25:15,620
Order! Order in the court!

577
00:25:15,750 --> 00:25:16,350
Order!

578
00:25:16,550 --> 00:25:17,200
Order!

579
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:20,480
Stop making noise!

580
00:25:20,480 --> 00:25:21,740
Maintain court order!

581
00:25:21,750 --> 00:25:23,000
Why is he tied up?

582
00:25:23,290 --> 00:25:24,000
Untie him.

583
00:25:27,790 --> 00:25:28,720
Let him sit down.

584
00:25:34,230 --> 00:25:35,290
Defendant's name?

585
00:25:35,590 --> 00:25:36,480
Qiao Zhiliang.

586
00:25:37,200 --> 00:25:38,160
Louder.

587
00:25:39,200 --> 00:25:39,720
Age?

588
00:25:40,510 --> 00:25:41,160
41.

589
00:25:41,590 --> 00:25:42,390
Home address?

590
00:25:43,030 --> 00:25:45,440
No. 3, Row 5, Staff Housing,

591
00:25:46,750 --> 00:25:47,240
Nanyu County No.1 High School.

592
00:25:47,240 --> 00:25:47,970
You scumbag!

593
00:25:48,040 --> 00:25:48,680
You've disgraced

594
00:25:48,680 --> 00:25:50,140
